{"content": "Here is the detailed analysis of the time complexity of Quicksort.\n\n### Summary of Time Complexity\n\n| Case | Time Complexity | Condition |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Best Case** | $O(n \\log n)$ | The pivot divides the array into two equal halves. |\n| **Average Case** | $O(n \\log n)$ | The pivot divides the array into reasonably balanced partitions. |\n| **Worst Case** | $O(n^2)$ | The pivot is always the smallest or largest element (e.g., sorted array). |\n\n---\n\n### Detailed Analysis\n\nQuicksort is a divide-and-conquer algorithm. Its time complexity is determined by the recurrence relation:\n$$T(n) = T(k", "reasoning": null, "logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.9759769357614729, "top_logprobs": [{"token": "Here", "logprob": -0.9759769357614729}, {"token": "To", "logprob": -1.3019428171091292}, {"token": "The", "logprob": -2.0959243692331526}, {"token": "###", "logprob": -2.4425868905954573}, {"token": "Qu", "logprob": -2.6679363168649886}, {"token": "Based", "logprob": -3.6740112222604964}, {"token": "#", "logprob": -3.867750159638426}, {"token": "**", "logprob": -4.911437980072996}, {"token": "##", "logprob": -4.93753623141577}, {"token": "Quick", "logprob": -4.96018027438452}, {"token": "Below", "logprob": -7.637491217988035}, {"token": "In", "logprob": -7.9326457895212386}, {"token": "This", "logprob": -8.009996405976317}, {"token": "An", "logprob": -8.716482154267332}, {"token": "Determin", "logprob": -8.882457724946043}, {"token": "For", "logprob": -8.97921275271704}, {"token": "Standard", "logprob": -9.023233405488035}, {"token": "Ass", "logprob": -9.085712424653074}, {"token": "qu", "logprob": -9.097978583710692}, {"token": "Since", "logprob": -9.20582007540991}]}, {"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0005055658531958329, "top_logprobs": [{"token": " is", "logprob": -0.0005055658531958329}, {"token": " are", "logprob": -7.724546550960618}, {"token": " represents", "logprob": -10.080476879329758}, {"token": " provides", "logprob": -